 became bowl eligible with a 60-29 win over UTSA on Thursday night","story":"BOCA RATON, Fla. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4869991/caden-veltkamp\" target=\"_new\">Caden Veltkamp</a> threw four touchdown passes, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5390418/leonard-farrow\" target=\"_new\">Leonard Farrow</a> ran for more than 100 yards and Florida Atlantic became bowl eligible with a 60-29 win over UTSA on Thursday night \n\n\r\n              It was the first conference loss this season for UTSA (7-2, 4-1 American Conference), which drops a half-game back of North Texas and into a second-place tie with Memphis. \n\n\r\n              Veltkamp was 17-of-25 passing for 210 yards and connected three times with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4914830/easton-messer\" target=\"_new\">Easton Messer</a> for scores. Messer had seven catches for 85 yards, and he also threw a touchdown pass for Florida Atlantic (6-3, 3-2 American Conference). \n\n\r\n              Farrow burst through the middle before slipping a tackle and running <a href=\"https://x.com/FAUFootball/status/2118549238053286167?a=qvKcAbRDlN--EKGpks9E&s=20\">59 yards into the end zone</a> to give FAU a 50-29 lead late in the third quarter. Farrow finished with 126 yards rushing on 12 carries. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5215500/ethan-ervin\" target=\"_new\">Ethan Ervin</a> ran 15 times for 92 yards. \n\n\r\n              The Owls generated 566 yards of offense, 342 on the ground. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4775136/owen-mccown\" target=\"_new\">Owen McCown</a> completed 20 of 35 passes for 265 yards and threw three TD passes for the Roadrunners. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4918111/a'marion-peterson\" target=\"_new\">A'Marion Peterson</a> had a 52-yard touchdown run and finished with 77 yards rushing. \n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              UTSA: Hosts North Texas on Nov. 14.\n\n\r\n              Florida Atlantic: At Tulsa on Nov. 14.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-06T05:05:33Z"}}